# Fifth Wheel March: the title. A trumpet's tune over the tuba's oom and the horns' pah, a snare marching; Bb
# major. A march's form (80 bars, about 2:50): a fanfare on the dominant, the first strain twice (A A'), the
# second (B B2), the trio in the subdominant (Eb) on a French horn, softly (C C'), a break of calls and drum
# rolls, the trio again grandioso with the trumpet an octave up, and a coda. Its end leads back to the start.
title Fifth Wheel March
tempo 112
meter 4/4
swing 0

